WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.100
Not everything in this world is exactly as
it seems.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:09.130
In fact, there are many creatures in the wild
that go out of their way to be deceptive,

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:14.120
to disguise themselves as something entirely
different from their true nature.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:18.710
Aggressive Mimicry refers to a phenomenon
in which predators or parasites take on the

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:24.550
appearance of something harmless or even appealing,
in order to lure in their intended prey or

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.699
host without detection.

00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:32.730
They might resemble food, an inanimate part
of the environment, or even a potential mate.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:36.950
Whatever they choose, they're secretly a wolf
in sheep's clothing.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.490
In the deep dark waters of the ocean, the
Anglerfish dangles an alluring light from

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:46.730
its head, ushering in little fish that it
can trap in its mouth and devour whole.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:51.390
The alligator snapping turtle wiggles its
long tongue like a worm, attractive hungry

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.540
fish looking for their next meal.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:58.320
Instead, they become the meal for something
bigger and more clever than them.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.150
False cleanerfish share the appearance of
another species, one that helps clean larger

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.689
fish in a symbiotic relationship.

00:01:05.689 --> 00:01:10.511
When the imposters find a victim, they swim
close under the pretense of cleaning, only

00:01:10.511 --> 00:01:13.790
to take a bite out of them and swim away.

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:16.759
Predators use similar illusions on land, too.

00:01:16.759 --> 00:01:22.060
Antimimicking jumping spiders wave their false
antennae in the air in an imitation of an

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.860
ant's movements, isolating the insects from
their colony before dragging them back to

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.720
their lair to be devoured.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:32.950
The mouthparts of the male spiders are shaped
like the head of an ant, but this imitation

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:38.270
head splits apart to reveal the spider's fangs,
and its true intentions.

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:43.200
The Photuris firefly lights up its body in
a mimicry of other firefly species' mating

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.310
signals, signaling male fireflies looking
for companionship.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:51.500
When they respond to the call however, they
will not find a willing mate waiting, but

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:55.790
instead a femme fatale of a firefly that just
wants to eat.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:02:00.710
The spider-tailed horned viper has a bulbous
tip on its tail, with false legs jutting out

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:02.340
on either side.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.150
As the snake wiggles its tail, running it
across the ground while the rest of its body

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:10.750
lies in wait just out of sight, a hungry bird
spots it from above.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:15.569
When the bird swoops down to seize the opportunity,
the snake reveals itself, snapping up the

00:02:15.569 --> 00:02:18.570
unfortunate bird before it can escape.

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:23.750
Thankfully, humans are so much smarter and
more observant than fish, ants, and birds.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:26.170
We're safe from this sort of trickery.

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:30.300
There aren't any animals out there who've
learned how to look like something familiar,

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:34.959
something everyday, just to put unsuspecting
people at ease and lure us into its waiting

00:02:34.959 --> 00:02:36.360
jaws...right?

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.780
Wrong.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:42.440
Only a couple of years ago, the SCP Foundation
discovered a being that has mastered aggressive

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:46.690
mimicry on a level previously unseen in the
natural world.

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:51.980
Unfortunately for us, its prey of choice happens
to be humans, and its hunting ground is the

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:58.019
very cities where we like to think we're safe
from something much bigger, meaner, and hungrier

00:02:58.019 --> 00:02:59.019
than us.

00:02:59.019 --> 00:03:02.660
A short video went viral on a popular social
media platform.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:07.090
The specific platform has been redacted from
official files, but the details of it are

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:12.650
clear: A popular creator on the app, a young
woman known for her makeup tutorials and restaurant

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:15.909
recommendations around her native city of
Los Angeles.

00:03:15.909 --> 00:03:19.810
She was live streaming and answering questions
while going about her day, when she stepped

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:23.580
onto a train at one of the Metro stations
around the city.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:27.940
The train was extremely crowded, and she was
preparing to end the live video, planning

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:30.660
to resume once she reached her destination.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:35.460
But just as she went to press the button and
end the stream, something strange happened.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:39.599
The train went dark, and the space flooded
with a strange, thick liquid.

00:03:39.599 --> 00:03:44.900
The girl screamed, in either pain, horror,
or both, and dropped the phone.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:49.030
Whatever it fell into must have degraded the
phone at an extremely rapid pace, because

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:52.890
the video feed cut out immediately after a
SPLASH!

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:57.540
All across social media, people shared the
video with one question in mind: What happened

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:58.920
on that train?

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:04.200
Fans mounted a campaign to find the influencer,
to help her if she was in any immediate danger,

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.459
but there were no leads.

00:04:06.459 --> 00:04:10.720
Her friends and family said she never came
home that day, and when authorities attempted

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:14.590
to trace her phone, they could not get any
kind of signal.

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:17.870
Becoming increasingly concerned about this
missing girl, and the possibility of some

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:23.139
kind of unreported train accident, authorities
contacted the Los Angeles Metro and showed

00:04:23.139 --> 00:04:24.690
them the video footage.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:28.200
But every train was accounted for and in pristine
condition.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:33.690
There had been no strange chemical leaks,
no crashes, and certainly nothing like what

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.130
the video appeared to show.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:39.840
At the same time, there were missing persons
reports being filed all across the country,

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:43.530
in every area with a thriving public transportation
system.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:48.010
Not only were the occupants of the Los Angeles
train unaccounted for, with no wreckage or

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:54.280
bodies to be found, but people were disappearing
in train stations in New York, Boston, Chicago,

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:56.730
Washington, D.C., and more.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:00.570
A woman reported her husband missing after
he called her to check in during his daily

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.220
commute home from work.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:07.130
The train had kept going for much longer than
it ordinarily did, drifting off of its usual

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:08.130
route.

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:12.200
He told her that something was wrong, that
he had a terrible feeling of foreboding, and

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:13.940
then the call cut off.

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:15.670
He never made it home for dinner.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:20.881
A young woman was on her way to start an internship
at a prestigious New York City magazine, but

00:05:20.881 --> 00:05:23.600
never arrived for her first meeting.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:27.280
When her would-be boss reached out to the
girl's roommate, all he knew was that she

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:29.700
had planned to take the train to work that
morning.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:34.639
A private detective trailing a man's wife
for him, looking for evidence of an affair,

00:05:34.639 --> 00:05:38.139
lost track of her when she stepped onto a
train downtown.

00:05:38.139 --> 00:05:42.311
He took the next train, hoping to catch her
at what he assumed would be her stop, but

00:05:42.311 --> 00:05:43.570
she never got off.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:48.100
He wasn't able to track her down, and had
to give her suspicious husband the news that

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:51.449
his wife had somehow vanished into thin air.

00:05:51.449 --> 00:05:55.139
It wasn't just one or two people every so
often, either.

00:05:55.139 --> 00:05:59.600
Entire train cars of people were just disappearing,
never to be seen again.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:05.729
No matter how hard anyone tried, they could
not find any answers, no logical explanation

00:06:05.729 --> 00:06:07.530
for what could have happened.

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:13.160
Fortunately, the video circulated so widely
that it made it onto the feed of an SCP Foundation

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:16.200
employee, who was idly scrolling during a
bathroom break.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:20.360
He was so shocked by what he saw that he almost
forgot to pull up his pants before running

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:21.890
out into the hall.

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:27.110
Fortunately, he did remember, and rushed to
his supervisor's office fully clothed.

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:30.900
After determining that the video was not a
hoax or some kind of viral marketing stunt

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:35.940
intended to sell a new brand of spicy chips,
the SCP Foundation decided to launch a formal

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:42.090
investigation into anomalous activity involving
trains and subway systems around the country.

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:46.009
Task forces were set up in every major city,
and field researchers were assigned to take

00:06:46.009 --> 00:06:49.680
the train all day, every day, as much as possible.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:53.650
As they did, they would maintain communication
with the head of their task force, who would

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:57.120
monitor their findings via hidden cameras
and microphones.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:02.000
A week passed without incident, and the Foundation
was starting to wonder if, somehow, the Los

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:07.759
Angeles video had been faked, when the Chicago
task force made a harrowing discovery.

00:07:07.759 --> 00:07:12.670
Officer Jamie Bower was assigned to monitor
the trains on Chicago's Blue Line, taking

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:16.780
the train throughout the day and keeping an
eye out for suspicious or potentially anomalous

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:17.940
activity.

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:21.060
One week in, and he pretty much had it down
to a basic routine.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:25.360
He would grab breakfast, hop on the train,
and enjoy his coffee and meal while reading

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:27.900
a book and riding the train to its last stop.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:31.639
Then, he'd pick up lunch and do the same thing
all over again.

00:07:31.639 --> 00:07:33.160
He'd have dinner, and repeat.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:38.260
It wasn't too exciting, but then again, excitement,
in this case, probably meant horrors beyond

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:39.260
his comprehension.

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:44.669
So, he was perfectly fine with traversing
the city in a subway car and catching up on

00:07:44.669 --> 00:07:48.069
the backlog of murder mysteries he'd been
meaning to read.

00:07:48.069 --> 00:07:53.069
It was Monday afternoon, he'd picked up a
slice of deep dish pizza, excited to try it

00:07:53.069 --> 00:07:57.960
for the first time, and walked down into the
metro station as he took his first bite.

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:01.340
"Can you try not to chew into your microphone,
please?

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:05.979
It's gross," Dr. Susan Shepherd, the head
of the Chicago task force, spoke into Jamie's

00:08:05.979 --> 00:08:06.979
earpiece.

00:08:06.979 --> 00:08:09.230
"You got it, boss," he said, his mouth full.

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:10.230
"Thanks.

00:08:10.230 --> 00:08:11.419
See anything unusual today?"

00:08:11.419 --> 00:08:12.419
she asked.

00:08:12.419 --> 00:08:13.419
"You tell me!

00:08:13.419 --> 00:08:14.450
You can see the video feed, right?"

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:17.160
He took another bite, chewing as quietly as
he could.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:18.750
"Sure, but you're there on the ground.

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:20.449
Just...keep an eye out, okay?

00:08:20.449 --> 00:08:23.889
Be careful, and remember to draw your weapon
if something goes south.

00:08:23.889 --> 00:08:27.389
Don't just disappear into your book and forget
to keep your wits about you," Dr. Shepherd

00:08:27.389 --> 00:08:28.389
sighed.

00:08:28.389 --> 00:08:29.389
"Yep!

00:08:29.389 --> 00:08:32.099
Getting on the train now, not going to talk
much so these folks don't think I'm nuts."

00:08:32.099 --> 00:08:36.410
Jamie waited for the doors to open, and for
just a moment, noticed that they seemed to

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:39.010
stick just a little this time.

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:41.099
Nothing to be too worried about, though.

00:08:41.099 --> 00:08:44.820
Everything looked normal, just as it had on
every other ride he'd taken.

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:49.470
He could feel the Agatha Christie book calling
to him from inside of his tote bag, and he

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:55.269
wanted to crack it open and see what clues
Hercule Poirot had come across, but Dr. Shepherd

00:08:55.269 --> 00:08:56.269
was right.

00:08:56.269 --> 00:08:57.839
He'd been slacking off.

00:08:57.839 --> 00:09:00.180
He needed to pay attention to his surroundings.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:02.050
So, he did just that.

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:05.390
He watched as the train car steadily filled
up with strangers.

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:09.650
College students with bags full of books and
exhausted expressions, middle-aged people

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:15.149
in business attire, tourists wearing souvenir
baseball caps, and snapping pictures of everything

00:09:15.149 --> 00:09:16.160
in sight.

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:20.070
Before too long, the train was completely
packed, and Jamie could barely move without

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:21.970
bumping elbows with someone.

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:26.190
It was a little claustrophobic, but that was
public transportation.

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:30.500
Jamie leaned back in his seat, pulled his
book out, and focused on the comforting rumble

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.560
of the engine, the rhythm of the wheels on
the tracks.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:36.680
Suddenly, without warning, the train screeched
to a stop.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:40.779
They were in the middle of a tunnel, Jamie
assumed, from the darkness that flanked them

00:09:40.779 --> 00:09:42.529
out the window on either side.

00:09:42.529 --> 00:09:43.529
Wait, was it dark?

00:09:43.529 --> 00:09:46.060
Or had the windows just...disappeared?

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:50.720
He squinted through the blackness and tried
to see what was outside, but he couldn't make

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.490
sense of his surroundings.

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:56.440
All around, the other passengers were becoming
restless, nervous.

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:59.300
Some were calling for help; others were just
complaining.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:00.300
"Doctor?

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:01.350
You seeing this?"

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:02.480
Jamie hissed into his microphone.

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:04.180
"I don't see a thing."

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:05.180
Dr. Shepherd replied.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:06.260
"Are you alright?"

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:07.649
"Fine, the train's just stalled.

00:10:07.649 --> 00:10:08.809
I don't know where.

00:10:08.809 --> 00:10:10.370
Or what's wrong with it."

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:13.550
Jamie began feeling along the walls of the
train, looking for the doors.

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:14.550
"Huh.

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:15.550
That's weird..."

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:16.550
"What?"

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.380
"Well, the crack in the doors, where they
come together, should be right here...But

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:19.890
it's all smooth.

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:22.070
No gaps or anything, like it's all one thing.

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:26.339
And it feels strange...like-" He cut himself
off as his stomach dropped, a sudden rush

00:10:26.339 --> 00:10:28.399
of fear flooding his senses.

00:10:28.399 --> 00:10:29.399
"Like what?"

00:10:29.399 --> 00:10:30.399
Dr. Shepherd pressed.

00:10:30.399 --> 00:10:33.420
"Like it's alive," Jamie said, shakily.

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:34.420
"Campbell.

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:35.420
What's happening in there?"

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:37.459
Dr. Shepherd began taking furious notes on
her end.

00:10:37.459 --> 00:10:38.459
"I don't know.

00:10:38.459 --> 00:10:39.779
It's so dark.

00:10:39.779 --> 00:10:40.779
Everyone's scared.

00:10:40.779 --> 00:10:41.779
I'm scared.

00:10:41.779 --> 00:10:45.639
I don't think this is a train, I don't know
what it is but it's nothing good..."

00:10:45.639 --> 00:10:50.510
As Jamie felt around, he smelled something
sour, foul, and sharp in his nose.

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:54.860
He heard liquid splashing onto the ground,
the sound of something sizzling.

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:57.250
And then people started to scream.

00:10:57.250 --> 00:11:01.960
As he felt along the wall, something dripped
onto his hand, and then it started to burn.

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:06.400
He cried out in agony as whatever had dripped
onto him ate away at the skin, dissolving

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:07.820
his hand bit by bit.

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:08.920
"What is it?"

00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:11.850
Dr. Shepherd's voice shook as she heard the
pain in Jamie's voice.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:17.899
"Some kind of acid, it's everywhere- It's
on the walls, the floor, it just keeps coming..."

00:11:17.899 --> 00:11:18.899
He trailed off.

00:11:18.899 --> 00:11:19.899
"Oh god, oh god.

00:11:19.899 --> 00:11:20.899
We're in a stomach.

00:11:20.899 --> 00:11:22.120
Whatever this is...it's eating us."

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:23.910
"Campbell, you need to get out of there.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:24.910
Right now!"

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:25.910
Dr. Shepherd ordered.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:26.910
"Draw your weapon.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.730
Whatever you need to do, just get out!"

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:32.910
Jamie pulled out his weapon and started firing
at the place where the doors should be, but

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:37.790
the bullets bounced off uselessly as if the
fleshy material was the side of a tank.

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:41.850
He fired until there was no more ammunition
left, and then he kept squeezing the trigger

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:44.589
some more out of pure survival instinct.

00:11:44.589 --> 00:11:49.160
But all it got him was a useless click, and
the certainty that the one thing he had brought

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:53.120
with him in case of emergency was completely
useless.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:57.820
All the while, the acid was creeping higher,
dripping from every surface, filling the train

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:03.240
car until it swallowed the cries for help
and screams of fear and agony.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:07.680
All Dr. Shepherd could do was listen, helpless,
as Jamie and the rest of the passengers were

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:10.700
digested inside of the massive stomach.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:15.360
What happened to Officer Jamie Campbell was
tragic, but it provided important information

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:18.720
that the Foundation would likely never have
gotten otherwise.

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:23.870
They now knew a few key things about this
new anomaly: it was some kind of living thing

00:12:23.870 --> 00:12:29.220
able to disguise itself as a train, it was
resilient to bullets and firearms, and it

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:32.490
was hiding in plain sight in order to hunt
human beings.

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:37.529
They had found the culprit for the rash of
mysterious disappearances, and it was a race

00:12:37.529 --> 00:12:43.590
of unidentified creatures capable of taking
on the shape of a common underground train.

00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:47.560
The newfound information quickly circulated
throughout the Foundation, making its way

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:53.810
to the various task forces assigned to Operation
Metro, as it had been unofficially nicknamed.

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:56.770
Task Force members were no longer instructed
to board trains.

00:12:56.770 --> 00:13:01.110
Instead, they would slip hidden cameras onto
as many train cars as they possibly could,

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:03.380
each outfitted with a tracking device.

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:07.680
Then, the Foundation could remotely monitor
the trains for any potential signs of the

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:13.089
mysterious creatures, looking for imposters
masquerading as trains, without unnecessarily

00:13:13.089 --> 00:13:15.300
losing any more operatives in action.

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:20.670
Now, as for what they would do once they found
one of these massive creatures was still uncertain,

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:23.360
but at least they had somewhere to start.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:28.050
The SCP Foundation tried and failed to contain
several instances of the carnivorous species

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:29.709
before they finally got it right.

00:13:29.709 --> 00:13:34.850
They attempted to freeze the inside of one
train with liquid nitrogen, hoping to incapacitate

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:39.310
the creature before it could feed, defend
itself, or escape custody.

00:13:39.310 --> 00:13:43.500
The extreme cold seemed to have no effect,
however, and the false train slammed its doors

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:47.970
shut at the first sign of discomfort, then
sped away at a high speed.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:51.630
As it did, the Task Force members noticed
that, though they could hear the sound of

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:56.140
wheels on the tracks, they could see legs
jutting out of the bottom of the creature,

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:57.500
scuttling along the ground.

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:01.740
Next, they attempted to take out the creature's
legs and render it immobile so that it could

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:02.769
be subdued.

00:14:02.769 --> 00:14:07.800
The legs were resilient to external damage,
becoming hard as rock whenever any weapon,

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:10.980
blade, or other implement made contact with
them.

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:15.110
One task force member tried to physically
hold some of the legs in place, but they shifted

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:20.259
their shape, becoming appendages resembling
tentacles, and threw the man out of the way

00:14:20.259 --> 00:14:23.550
before the false train hurried out of the
tunnel and out of sight.

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:28.050
They were able to track down a predatory train
just after a feeding, when it was slightly

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:30.070
sluggish after a large meal.

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:34.949
They pumped an aerosolized poison into the
train's interior, the belly of the beast,

00:14:34.949 --> 00:14:38.949
potent enough to take out a dinosaur, and
were relieved to find that the creature was

00:14:38.949 --> 00:14:40.370
unable to flee.

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:45.330
Unfortunately, though they were able to subdue
the creature, they killed it in the process.

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:49.980
At first, they assumed it was just inactive,
but it never resumed activity again.

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:53.910
It was just like an ordinary train car...almost.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:58.440
When the interior was touched, it felt warm
and slightly pliable, less like metal and

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:01.000
plastic and more like flesh.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:05.610
The longer the creature was still, the more
the windows on the sides stopped looking like

00:15:05.610 --> 00:15:09.339
windows and started looking like wide, glassy
eyes.

00:15:09.339 --> 00:15:13.769
The front of the train became a gaping maw,
the silhouette of the conductor inside revealed

00:15:13.769 --> 00:15:17.860
as an extension of the creature's body, resembling
a tongue.

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:22.399
Survivors and witnesses were given an amnestic
to remove any memories of the supposed "killer

00:15:22.399 --> 00:15:27.139
trains" running under their city, and the
Foundation prepared to bring the dead specimen

00:15:27.139 --> 00:15:28.630
in for further study.

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:33.160
A cover story was used involving massive repairs
to the train system, and, while the tunnels

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:38.199
were closed off, they managed to remove the
creature and transport it to a nearby Foundation

00:15:38.199 --> 00:15:39.290
Containment Site.

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:43.980
There, it was given one of the most extensive
autopsies in Foundation history, and the first

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:47.440
one conducted largely from inside of the subject.

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:52.040
The autopsy provided a more in-depth look
at the nature of the bizarre creature, and

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:53.620
its curious nature.

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:57.790
The creature, nicknamed the "train eater,"
referring to its preferred disguise and favorite

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:02.949
activity, was one of an apparent species of
carnivorous predators that used shapeshifting

00:16:02.949 --> 00:16:08.240
and an advanced form of aggressive mimicry
to prey on commuters, tourists, and anyone

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:11.290
else in need of a ride from one place to the
next.

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:17.040
It would mimic the shape, feel, and sounds
of a train, welcoming unassuming victims into

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:22.050
its stomach, and, once it was completely full
and able to efficiently feed, it would release

00:16:22.050 --> 00:16:26.990
an incredibly potent stomach acid into the
compartment and quickly dissolve everything

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:28.410
inside.

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:33.050
The creature was highly adaptable, able to
harden parts of its body at will and display

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:36.180
extreme resilience to weapons of any kind.

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:40.949
Due to this nearly impenetrable flesh, victims
trapped inside would be unable to force their

00:16:40.949 --> 00:16:42.120
way out.

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:46.649
As the research staff turned in their autopsy
results and official report, there was a sense

00:16:46.649 --> 00:16:52.569
of unease in the air as everyone wondered:
how many of these things are out there?

00:16:52.569 --> 00:16:55.529
Which innocent trip to work might be their
last?

00:16:55.529 --> 00:17:01.140
And how on earth could they hope to contain
something that could exist in endless numbers,

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:03.769
something so expert at hiding in plain sight?

00:17:03.769 --> 00:17:08.630
There was no realistic way to bring all of
these creatures into custody, and so they

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:12.370
would have to neutralize as many as possible
without being detected.

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:15.920
Foundation operatives embedded in various
city and state governments introduced new

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:21.669
measures to renovate public transportation
systems, including new sanitation protocols.

00:17:21.669 --> 00:17:26.500
As part of these protocols, all trains would
be sprayed with a high-strength "disinfectant"

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:28.449
before they could be certified for use.

00:17:28.449 --> 00:17:33.049
In reality, this disinfectant would be the
same poison used to take down the first Train

00:17:33.049 --> 00:17:35.090
Eater the Foundation studied.

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:38.980
Once any and all potential threats had been
rendered harmless, trains that were found

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:44.059
to be formerly living would be converted into
fully functioning trains, and allowed to run

00:17:44.059 --> 00:17:48.340
as normal in order to avoid unnecessary interruptions
to the public.

00:17:48.340 --> 00:17:52.590
In addition to these containment measures,
the Foundation monitors all social media for

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:57.730
mentions of unusual activity on trains, or
mentions of any more missing persons lost

00:17:57.730 --> 00:17:59.289
at metro stations.

00:17:59.289 --> 00:18:04.600
The original Los Angeles video that started
it all was scrubbed from the internet entirely.

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:09.330
So by all means, take advantage of your local
public transportation options, but remain

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:11.990
vigilant and keep your wits about you.

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:16.150
And remember next time you travel by train,
if you see something?

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:17.320
Say something.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:21.500
More specifically, if you see something unusual
on a train, if it looks a little different

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:26.590
than it did yesterday, if its sounds don't
seem quite right, make sure to let everyone

00:18:26.590 --> 00:18:31.790
around you know that it is not safe to be
here, and quickly make your way to the exit.

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:34.850
Then, maybe walk to your destination instead.

00:18:34.850 --> 00:18:39.289
It might make you a little bit late, but hey,
better late than dinner.

00:18:39.289 --> 00:18:45.390
Now go check out “SCP-342 - A Ticket to
Ride” and “SCP-2086 Man Eating Bus”

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:47.920
for more perilous anomalies on public transport!

